Privacy Policy for WiFi Password Generator

Last updated: June 2, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how the "WiFi Password Generator" mobile application ("the App", "we", "us") handles your information. By using the App, you agree to this policy.

1. Summary
WiFi Password Generator is designed to be private by default. All passwords and passphrases are generated and stored entirely on your device. We do not operate servers, and we do not collect, sell, or rent your personal data. (See "Advertising" below for third-party ads we may show in the future.)

2. Information We Collect
We do not collect any personal information ourselves. Specifically:
- Passwords and passphrases you generate are created on your device and are never sent to us or any third party.
- Your saved/copied history is stored locally on your device only, and you can delete it at any time from within the App.
- Network names (SSID) and passwords you enter to create a Wi-Fi QR code are processed on your device only and are not transmitted to us.
We have no access to any of this information.

3. Permissions
The current version of the App requests no sensitive permissions. It does not request access to the internet, your location, contacts, storage, or camera. Saving a QR-code image uses the system media APIs (scoped storage) and does not require a storage permission.

4. Advertising (third-party services)
A future version of the App may display advertisements provided by third-party advertising networks, such as Google AdMob. When ads are enabled, these networks may automatically collect and process certain information in order to serve and measure ads, including:
- a device advertising identifier (Advertising ID),
- IP address and the approximate (coarse) location derived from it,
- device information (model, operating system, language), and
- app usage and ad-interaction data.
This information is collected directly by the advertising provider under its own privacy policy. For Google AdMob, see Google's Privacy Policy (https://policies.google.com/privacy) and "How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services" (https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites). We will update this Privacy Policy and our Google Play "Data safety" disclosures before enabling ads.
You can limit ad personalization at any time on Android via Settings → Privacy → Ads → Reset/Delete advertising ID.

5. Children's Privacy
The App is not directed to children under 13 (or the equivalent minimum age in your jurisdiction), and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If ads are shown, they will be configured in accordance with applicable policies (e.g., Google Play Families and AdMob requirements).

6. Data Security & Retention
Because your data stays on your device, its security depends on your device's own protections. Generated passwords and history remain on your device until you delete them or uninstall the App. Uninstalling the App removes all locally stored data.

7. Your Choices
- Clear your generated history any time from the History screen in the App.
- Reset or delete your Advertising ID in your device settings.
- Uninstall the App to remove all locally stored data.

8. Changes to This Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes (for example, when advertising is introduced) will be reflected here with an updated "Last updated" date and in the Google Play "Data safety" section.
